WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.106
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C one, Book four.

2
00:00:05.406 --> 00:00:08.967
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:17.213
Unit fourteen: Digital Transformation. Today you will describe organisational change with from X toward Y movement language.

4
00:00:17.513 --> 00:00:20.317
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:24.453
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:26.910
Digital transformation.

7
00:00:27.917 --> 00:00:33.643
Digital transformation means the integration of digital technology into all areas of a business.

8
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:37.991
Digital transformation changed how the ministry serves citizens.

9
00:00:38.583 --> 00:00:41.538
Your turn. Say: Digital transformation.

10
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.225
Digital transformation.

11
00:00:46.983 --> 00:00:48.298
Legacy system.

12
00:00:49.283 --> 00:00:54.209
Legacy system means old technology still in use that is hard to replace.

13
00:00:54.817 --> 00:00:58.082
The bank's legacy system could not support mobile apps.

14
00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:01.463
Your turn. Say: Legacy system.

15
00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.707
Legacy system.

16
00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:07.718
Cloud migration.

17
00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:12.655
Cloud migration means moving data and software to online servers.

18
00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:16.004
Cloud migration cut their IT costs by a third.

19
00:01:16.617 --> 00:01:19.675
Your turn. Say: Cloud migration.

20
00:01:22.533 --> 00:01:24.127
Cloud migration.

21
00:01:24.883 --> 00:01:25.896
Automation.

22
00:01:26.883 --> 00:01:31.286
Automation means the use of technology to perform tasks without human effort.

23
00:01:31.883 --> 00:01:34.696
Automation reduced invoice errors dramatically.

24
00:01:35.283 --> 00:01:37.645
Your turn. Say: Automation.

25
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.478
Automation.

26
00:01:42.217 --> 00:01:43.427
Digital-first.

27
00:01:44.417 --> 00:01:47.821
Digital-first means designed primarily for digital channels.

28
00:01:48.417 --> 00:01:51.798
The insurer adopted a digital-first approach to claims.

29
00:01:52.383 --> 00:01:55.674
Your turn. Say: Digital-first.

30
00:01:58.533 --> 00:01:59.697
Digital-first.

31
00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:01.753
Change management.

32
00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:06.387
Change management means guiding people through organisational change.

33
00:02:06.983 --> 00:02:09.703
Good change management reduced staff resistance.

34
00:02:10.317 --> 00:02:13.364
Your turn. Say: Change management.

35
00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.607
Change management.

36
00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:19.386
Data-driven.

37
00:02:20.383 --> 00:02:24.368
Data-driven means based on data analysis rather than intuition.

38
00:02:24.983 --> 00:02:27.308
Data-driven decisions replaced guesswork.

39
00:02:27.917 --> 00:02:30.383
Your turn. Say: Data-driven.

40
00:02:33.233 --> 00:02:34.362
Data-driven.

41
00:02:35.117 --> 00:02:36.153
Agility.

42
00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:40.369
Agility means the ability to respond quickly to change.

43
00:02:40.983 --> 00:02:43.169
Cloud tools gave the team new agility.

44
00:02:43.783 --> 00:02:46.053
Your turn. Say: Agility.

45
00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:50.157
Agility.

46
00:02:50.967 --> 00:02:54.652
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:55.517 --> 00:03:01.164
Visal, the electricity company still records meter readings on paper. How would you modernise it?

48
00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:08.986
I'd move it gradually from paper records toward a digital system, starting with smart meters in Phnom Penh.

49
00:03:10.083 --> 00:03:12.269
Why not replace everything at once?

50
00:03:13.383 --> 00:03:23.756
Because the legacy system holds decades of data. Shifting from manual processes toward automation too quickly could cause billing chaos.

51
00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:26.757
And the staff who read meters?

52
00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:35.344
Change management is essential. We'd retrain them, moving their roles away from data collection toward customer service.

53
00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.093
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:42.575
Grammar focus: From X toward Y movement language.

55
00:03:42.875 --> 00:03:44.004
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:44.717 --> 00:03:48.551
Companies move from legacy systems toward cloud infrastructure.

57
00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:52.866
The bank is shifting from branch visits toward mobile services.

58
00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:57.143
Staff roles moved away from data entry toward customer care.

59
00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:07.057
'Toward(s)' suggests direction and gradual progress; 'to' suggests reaching the end point. Do not combine them: 'toward the cloud', not 'toward to the cloud'.

60
00:04:07.817 --> 00:04:11.409
Be careful! Don't say: They moved from paper toward to cloud.

61
00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:15.889
Say: They moved from paper toward the cloud.

62
00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:17.991
From X toward Y (no 'to').

63
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.754
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:24.276
More Than New Technology.

65
00:04:24.576 --> 00:04:32.439
Digital transformation describes an organisation's shift from manual, paper-based processes toward integrated digital operations.

66
00:04:33.433 --> 00:04:40.808
Many projects fail not because the technology is poor, but because employees resist changes to familiar routines.

67
00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:49.291
Replacing legacy systems is especially risky, since old databases often contain data that no one fully understands.

68
00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:57.350
Successful firms therefore move step by step from pilot projects toward company-wide adoption, investing heavily in training.

69
00:04:58.333 --> 00:05:05.569
Cambodia's rapid move from cash toward QR payments shows how quickly behaviour can change once a system is genuinely convenient.

70
00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:10.668
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:11.517 --> 00:05:14.851
The school moved blank paper exams toward online tests.

72
00:05:15.151 --> 00:05:18.131
A, from. B, of. C, out.

73
00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:23.388
The answer is A: from.

74
00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.873
Old technology that is hard to replace is a blank.

75
00:05:28.173 --> 00:05:33.022
A, cloud migration. B, legacy system. C, digital-first.

76
00:05:36.567 --> 00:05:39.193
The answer is B: legacy system.

77
00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:43.290
Guiding people through organisational change is blank.

78
00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:47.859
A, automation. B, agility. C, change management.

79
00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:53.806
The answer is C: change management.

80
00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:56.752
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:57.052 --> 00:06:05.361
A, We are moving toward to cloud storage.. B, We are moving toward cloud storage.. C, We are moving from toward cloud storage..

82
00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:11.817
The answer is B: We are moving toward cloud storage..

83
00:06:12.983 --> 00:06:16.237
According to the reading, many digital projects fail because…

84
00:06:16.537 --> 00:06:22.013
A, employees resist change. B, computers are too slow. C, data is too cheap.

85
00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:28.483
The answer is A: employees resist change.

86
00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:33.049
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:33.883 --> 00:06:37.543
What challenge might a company face when replacing a legacy system?

88
00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:55.723
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:56.023 --> 00:07:31.353
One major challenge is migrating data safely. A legacy system may hold years of customer records in outdated formats, and moving them from the old platform toward a new one can introduce errors. Another challenge is people: employees who have used the old system for decades may resist learning new procedures. If a bank's new software miscalculates balances, customers lose trust immediately. Therefore, I believe companies should test carefully, run both systems in parallel for a period and train staff thoroughly.

90
00:07:31.653 --> 00:07:33.606
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:34.517 --> 00:07:39.468
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and from x toward y movement language.

92
00:07:39.768 --> 00:07:44.672
Today's value is adaptability. Be ready for rain or sun and change your plans.

93
00:07:44.972 --> 00:07:47.648
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

94
00:07:47.948 --> 00:07:51.285
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

